 * studentName
 * rollNumber
 * totalMarks (int) - Calculated by you
 * percentage (double) - Calculated by you
 * finalResult (String) - Calculated by you
 * The List:
   @OneToMany(cascade = CascadeType.ALL)
@JoinColumn(name = "fk_student_id")
private List<SubjectMark> subjects;

4️⃣ The Service Layer Algorithm (Your Task) 📝
This is where you need to focus. Here is the pseudo-code logic you need to write in Java:
 * Create StudentResult object.
 * Set Name and Roll Number from Request.
 * Set the List (student.setSubjects(...)).
 * Initialize Variables:
   * double total = 0;
   * boolean hasFailed = false; (A flag to track if they failed any subject).
 * The Loop (for (SubjectMark sub : request.getSubjects())):
   * Add marks to total.
   * Check: if (sub.getMarks() < 35) -> Set hasFailed = true.
 * After the Loop:
   * Set student.setTotalMarks(total).
   * Calculate Percentage: (total / (number of subjects * 100)) * 100.
   * Final Logic:
     * if (hasFailed) -> Status = "FAIL".
     * else if (percentage >= 75) -> Status = "DISTINCTION".
     * (etc...)
 * Save and Return.
